/-!
# Checked blocks of the degree-1242 column inverse product

Every literal inverse coefficient is checked against the original table, and
its packed product is checked against the corresponding identity row. Separate
row declarations keep the numerical checks small; blocks of at most 32 expose
these checks to the final coverage proof in `Certificates.ColumnInverse`.

Source: `../../source/README.md`; original ATLAS degree-1242 matrices;
James, J. Algebra 27 (1973), 57–111. Arithmetic inputs are generated by
`../../source/generate.py`, family `ColumnInverse`.
-/

-- The bounded measurements in ColumnInverse/source/README.md justify this option.
set_option Elab.async false

